#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:1
msgid "Running the analyzer within Xcode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:4
msgid ""
"Since Xcode 3.2, users have been able to run the static analyzer [directly "
"within Xcode](https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/recipes/xcode_help-"
"source_editor/chapters/Analyze.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40009975-CH4-SW1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:6
msgid ""
"It integrates directly with the Xcode build system and presents analysis "
"results directly within Xcode's editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:8
msgid "Can I use the open source analyzer builds with Xcode?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:10
msgid "**Yes**. Instructions are included below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:15
msgid "**Viewing static analyzer results in Xcode**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:17
msgid "Key features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:19
msgid ""
"**Integrated workflow:** Results are integrated within Xcode. There is no "
"experience of using a separate tool, and activating the analyzer requires a "
"single keystroke or mouse click."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:20
msgid ""
"**Transparency:** Works effortlessly with Xcode projects (including iPhone "
"projects)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:21
msgid ""
"**Cons:** Doesn't work well with non-Xcode projects. For those, consider "
"{doc}`CommandLineUsage`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:23
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:25
msgid ""
"Xcode is available as a free download from Apple on the [Mac App Store]"
"(https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/xcode/id497799835?mt=12), with "
"[instructions available](https://developer.apple.com/library/ios/recipes/"
"xcode_help-source_editor/chapters/Analyze.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/"
"TP40009975-CH4-SW1) for using the analyzer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:27
msgid "Using open source analyzer builds with Xcode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:29
msgid ""
"By default, Xcode uses the version of `clang` that came bundled with it to "
"analyze your code. It is possible to change Xcode's behavior to use an "
"alternate version of `clang` for this purpose while continuing to use the "
"`clang` that came with Xcode for compiling projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:31
msgid "Why try open source builds?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:33
msgid ""
"The advantage of using open source analyzer builds (provided on this "
"website) is that they are often newer than the analyzer provided with Xcode, "
"and thus can contain bug fixes, new checks, or simply better analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:35
msgid ""
"On the other hand, new checks can be experimental, with results of variable "
"quality. Users are encouraged to file bug reports (for any version of the "
"analyzer) where they encounter false positives or other issues here: {doc}"
"`FilingBugs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:37
msgid "set-xcode-analyzer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:39
msgid ""
"Starting with analyzer build checker-234, analyzer builds contain a command "
"line utility called `set-xcode-analyzer` that allows users to change what "
"copy of `clang` that Xcode uses for analysis:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:53
msgid ""
"Operationally, **set-xcode-analyzer** edits Xcode's configuration files to "
"point it to use the version of `clang` you specify for static analysis. "
"Within this model it provides you two basic modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:55
msgid ""
"**--use-xcode-clang:** Switch Xcode (back) to using the `clang` that came "
"bundled with it for static analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:56
msgid ""
"**--use-checker-build:** Switch Xcode to using the `clang` provided by the "
"specified analyzer build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:58
msgid "Things to keep in mind"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:60
msgid "You should quit Xcode prior to running `set-xcode-analyzer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../analyzer/user-docs/UsingWithXCode.md:61
msgid ""
"You will need to run `set-xcode-analyzer` under **`sudo`** in order to have "
"write privileges to modify the Xcode configuration files."
msgstr ""

